From: Steeven Belvinos Affognon <belvinos@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] MILPSolver: fix set_par overload hiding that breaks SDDP on HiGHS

Declaring set_par( idx_type , int ) in MILPSolver hides ALL base-class set_par
overloads (C++ name hiding). The double overload is commented out and there was
no using-declaration, so MILPSolver had no double overload at all - neither
declared nor inherited.

Consequently HiGHSMILPSolver::set_par( par , double ), whose last statement is

    MILPSolver::set_par( par , value );      // value is a double

had no double overload to bind to. The compiler narrowed the double to int and
dispatched to set_par( idx_type , int ).

The int and double parameter enums are SEPARATE index spaces. In the stock
toyDataset, uc_solverconfig.txt contains

    dblAAccSol 5e-04                         # double parameter, index 7

which truncated to int 0 and silently overwrote

    intRelaxIntVars                          # int parameter, index 7

leaving relax_int_vars = false. The unit-commitment subproblem was therefore
solved as a MIP (204 integer variables, 187 binary). A MIP has no dual solution,
so HiGHSMILPSolver::has_dual_solution() returned false via
kHighsSolutionStatusNone, BendersBFunction::has_linearization( true ) returned
false, and SDDPSolver::SDDPOptimizer::oneStepBackward threw

    "SDDPOptimizer::oneStepBackward: no linearization is available."

This blocked the entire Plan4RES workflow on open-source-solver builds: SSV
failed, and SIM and CEM then failed because they consume SSV's Bellman values.

The fix restores the base-class overloads with a using-declaration.

Verified on the stock toyDataset, HiGHS 1.15.1, no commercial solver:

  before:  Solving MIP ... 204 integer variables (187 binary)
           terminate called: no linearization is available.  Aborted.

  after:   relax_int_vars=1
           Solving LP  (203 LP solves, 0 MIP)
           Backward value: 32818090192.099266052
           Forward value:  37582251925.978507996
           Optimal solution found.            exit code 0

  p4r SSV toyDataset now completes and writes results_simul/cuts.txt
  (real Bellman cuts) on a HiGHS-only build.
---
 MILPSolver/include/MILPSolver.h | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/MILPSolver/include/MILPSolver.h b/MILPSolver/include/MILPSolver.h
--- a/MILPSolver/include/MILPSolver.h
+++ b/MILPSolver/include/MILPSolver.h
@@ -531,6 +531,9 @@
  /// sets an integer parameter with the given value
+ /* Declaring any set_par() here hides ALL base-class set_par() overloads.
+  * Without this using-declaration a set_par( par , <double> ) call narrows the
+  * double to int and lands on the int overload, whose enum is a separate index
+  * space - silently corrupting an unrelated parameter. */
+ using CDASolver::set_par;
  void set_par( idx_type par , int value ) override;
 
  // sets a double parameter with the given value
  // void set_par( idx_type par , double value ) override;
